=== REASONING ===
ADR-015 invariants this slice MUST preserve (P1–P10 + W1):
  I1  default-off:     registry entry sets DefaultOn:false; integration test
                       proves the SPA component is absent and the backend
                       route 404s when ai_mode='off'.
  I3  baseline intact: AlertStudioPage's manual editor + Save path is
                       untouched. Apply-to-form copies the typed proposal
                       into setEditor; the existing baseline Save remains
                       the sole write path. AI never calls /api/v1/alerts
                       directly (propose-only contract).
  I4  zero egress:     ai-eval gate runs on the canned mock provider only;
                       off-mode test proves no ai/_internal egress is
                       triggered.
  I5  hidden UI:       withAiFeature('alert-tuning-suggestions', ...)
                       returns null when guard is off; Off-mode tests
                       assert queryByTestId('ai-feature-alert-tuning-
                       suggestions-root') is null.
  I6  404 routes:      Test verifies the registry-listed backend route
                       returns 404 when ai_mode='off' AND when the
                       per-feature toggle is off (I7).
  I7  per-feature:     Test toggles only alert-tuning-suggestions off
                       while keeping ai_mode='cloud' and proves the route
                       still 404s.
  I10 type system:     The strategy emits a typed AlertRulePatch envelope
                       through the draft_alert_rule_patch tool; the SPA
                       parses ev.data via a typed assertion to
                       AlertRuleDraftPatch; tsc --noEmit clean.
  I12 client/bg:       No background jobs / push kinds added (registry
                       JobNames=[], PushKinds=[]). Service-worker chunk
                       and storage key are scoped to the
                       alert-tuning-suggestions feature.

Decorator + dispatcher selection: the strategy declares
RedactionPolicy=PolicyAlertBuilder (deny-all) and Tools=
["draft_alert_rule_patch","validate_alert_rule"]. This routes through the
locked decorator chain (redaction → rate limit → cost cap → audit → trace)
without bypass. The strategy's tool selector (Tool.Name() switch) prevents
the LLM from inventing other tool calls.

Selection mechanism (P10 baseline coexistence): the AI feature is
mounted only when settings.ai_mode!='off' AND
ai_features.alert-tuning-suggestions==true. Both at the SPA boundary
(withAiFeature HOC) and at the backend boundary (ai.GuardedHandler).
The "manual tuning" baseline = AlertStudioPage's existing editor; AI
adds a sibling block that ends with "Apply to form" → setEditor →
existing Save path. There is no conditional inside business logic.

W1 inline wiring: the AIAlertTuningSuggestions component imports
useAiStream + AiOutputPanel, has a computed-disabled primary button,
calls cancel + reset on ruleId change via a dedicated effect that
captures stream.cancel via a stable destructure to avoid the
"identity-changes-each-render" bug, and contains zero placeholder
strings. The on-mode wiring test proves: exactly-one POST against the
registered route, delta text rendered inside the AI panel via the
data-testid root marker, double-submit no-op while streaming, and that
"Apply to form" copies the typed proposal into setEditor (verified by
spying on the baseline form's Save click landing the new value via
useUpdateAlertRule).

=== CHANGES ===
Production:
  + internal/ai/strategies/alert-tuning-suggestions/strategy.go
       FeatureID, system prompt (propose-only, refuse cross-rule),
       tool selector, RedactionPolicy=PolicyAlertBuilder.
  + internal/ai/strategies/alert-tuning-suggestions/goldens.yaml
       3 deterministic goldens (typical noisy threshold, insufficient
       history → unable_to_propose, refusal on other-rule mention).
  + internal/ai/strategies/alert-tuning-suggestions/canned/*.yaml
       3 canned mock-provider replies aligned with the goldens above.
  + internal/ai/tools/alert_tuning.go
       draft_alert_rule_patch tool: reads (rule, history) via narrow
       AlertHistoryReader port, returns typed envelope
       {rule_before, proposed{threshold,cooldown_min,severity,
       trigger_mode}, history_summary{firings_30d, median_interval_min,
       false_positive_ratio}, status, validation_error}. Validate()
       enforces explicit pointer-aware range checks for cooldown_min
       (1..1440) since the validate framework cannot deref *int via
       reflection.
  + internal/api/ai_alert_tuning_handler.go
       AIAlertTuningSource production adapter (uses AlertRuleRepo +
       AlertEventsRepo) and AlertTuningHandler (ai.GuardedHandler-wrapped,
       parses {ruleID} from URL, optional vehicle_id from body, dispatches
       to strategy via dispatch.Dispatcher). errors.Is(err, io.EOF)
       handles empty body without a stub helper.

